Z||000009||Oreif||03-12-2001||11:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by saleenfiero:<BR><B>Screwed up my wording there.  I meant what are the stocker ALTERNATORS rated at and what is safe to run with it for now?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>V-6 86 SE's came with 90 amp alt's. You can most likely be safe for now, Just don't run lights/high beams, fan on high, A/C, and stereo cranked. Also if you can get an alt from the junkyard then have it rewound so you just swap when you have time.<BR>||||reg||1
